invariant: INV-4
file: drbg.c
catches: drbg_test
reason: ch_drbg_seed takes a 31-byte seed, one byte under
  CH_DRBG_SEED_MIN, so a caller that passes a short buffer by mistake
  gets a running generator instead of a fault. bin/drbg_test passes
  exactly 31 bytes and requires CH_ASSERT to fire.

--- old
    CH_ASSERT(seed_len >= CH_DRBG_SEED_MIN); // a short seed is a programmer error (drbg.h)
--- new
    CH_ASSERT(seed_len >= CH_DRBG_SEED_MIN - 1); // a short seed is a programmer error (drbg.h)
